{"story_id":"IN-58816-001","title":"The Dead Man's Ring","title_raw":"THE DEAD MAN'S RING","notes":"","language":"en","original_language":"und","country":"India","country_code":"IN","culture_region":"ヒマラヤ山麓","latitude":31.1,"longitude":77.2,"location_precision":"culture_region","map_location_type":"source_culture_region","collector":"Alice Elizabeth Dracott","translator":null,"publication_year":1906,"year_evidence":"扉に 1906(序文は 1905 年 4 月の採録に触れる)","book_id":"PG-58816","book_title":"Simla Village Tales, or Folk Tales from the Himalayas","source_provider":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/58816","source_title":"Simla Village Tales; Or, Folk Tales from the Himalayas","license_status":"PUBLIC_DOMAIN_US","license_name":"Public Domain (United States)","license_jurisdiction":"US","rights_evidence_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/58816","redistribution_allowed":true,"commercial_use":true,"derivative_use":true,"ml_processing_status":"reviewed","verification_date":"2026-09-08","word_count":263,"text":"A young married woman one night listened to the jackals' cry, and heard\nthem say: \"Near the river lies a dead man; go and look on his finger\nand you will find a ring worth nine lakhs of rupees.\" She therefore\nrose and went to the riverside, not knowing that her husband secretly\nfollowed in her footsteps. Arrived there, she found the dead man, but\nthe ring was difficult to remove, so she drew it off with her teeth.\n\nHer husband, who did not know she had understood and acted upon the\ncry of the jackals, was horrified, and thought she was eating the flesh\nof the dead man; so he returned home, and when the morning came, took\nhis wife to her mother, and said: \"I have brought back your daughter,\nand refuse to live with her any longer, lest I come to some evil\nend.\" He gave no reason for having thus said, and returned to his home.\n\nIn the evening his wife sat sorrowfully in the garden of her father's\nhouse, and the crows came to roost in the peepul trees; and as they\ncame, they said: \"In this place are buried four boxes containing\nhidden treasure: dig and find it, O my daughter.\" The young girl\ncalled her parents and told them the message of the crows. At first\nthey laughed, but, after a while, they dug as she directed, and found\ntreasure which enriched the whole family. The girl then explained the\nstory of the dead man's ring, and her husband gladly forgave her and\nreceived her back.","cluster":7,"analysis":{"analysis_version":"1.0","embedding_model":"intfloat/multilingual-e5-small","themes":[{"label":"家族","z":0.462,"strength":"弱","confidence":0.614,"method":"embedding"}],"motifs":[{"label":"財宝獲得","z":0.583,"strength":"弱","confidence":0.642,"method":"embedding"}],"animals":[{"label":"烏","count":2,"method":"count","confidence":1.0}],"nature":[{"label":"川","count":1,"method":"count","confidence":1.0},{"label":"木","count":1,"method":"count","confidence":1.0}],"events":[{"position":0.0,"label":"Marriage","hits":1,"lift":73.08,"method":"count"},{"position":0.091,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.182,"label":"Death","hits":1,"lift":43.29,"method":"count"},{"position":0.273,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.364,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.455,"label":"Return","hits":1,"lift":105.19,"method":"count"},{"position":0.545,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.636,"label":"Return","hits":1,"lift":105.19,"method":"count"},{"position":0.727,"label":"Family","hits":1,"lift":11.22,"method":"count"},{"position":0.818,"label":"Reward","hits":1,"lift":146.36,"method":"count"},{"position":0.909,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":1.0,"label":"Reward","hits":1,"lift":96.05,"method":"count"}],"tension":[{"position":0.0,"tension":0.0,"raw":-4.762,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.091,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.182,"tension